        "text": "All the requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] submit_transcription.py** - Submits an audio file for batch transcription using AWS Transcribe.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] poll_transcription.py** - Polls a transcription job and returns the transcript using AWS Transcribe.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] diarized_transcript.py** - Requests speaker diarization for a recorded meeting using AWS Transcribe.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] timestamped_transcript.py** - Returns word or segment timestamps from a transcription result using AWS Transcribe.\n5. **[HELPER] speech_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Batch Speech-to-Text using AWS Transcribe.\n6. **[HELPER] speech_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Batch Speech-to-Text using AWS Transcribe.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] translate_transcript.py** - Translates completed transcript segments using AWS Translate.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] moderate_transcript.py** - Moderates transcript text before publishing using a simple regex replacement.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] archive_summary.py** - Summarizes transcription results using AWS Comprehend.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] transcript_embedding.py** - Embeds transcript segments for semantic retrieval using AWS SageMaker.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS as the concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities.",
